# Development Workflow

> **Reference**: Follow [tasklist.md](./tasklist.md) strictly. See [vision.md](../vision.md) for architecture and [conventions.md](../conventions.md) for code rules.

## Workflow Rules

### Before Starting Work
1. Review current iteration in [tasklist.md](./tasklist.md)
2. Check progress report status
3. Read relevant sections in [vision.md](../vision.md)

### Iteration Workflow

#### Step 1: Propose Solution
- Analyze iteration requirements
- Propose implementation approach
- Provide code snippets for key components
- Explain how it fits the architecture
- **Wait for approval before implementing**

#### Step 2: Implement
- Write code following [conventions.md](../conventions.md)
- Keep it simple (KISS principle)
- Implement only approved solution
- **Wait for confirmation after implementation**

#### Step 3: Test
- Verify test criteria from tasklist
- Ensure functionality works as expected
- Fix any issues found

#### Step 4: Update Progress
- Mark completed tasks with ✅ in [tasklist.md](./tasklist.md)
- Update progress report table status
- Add completion date if finished

#### Step 5: Commit
- Commit changes to repository
- Use clear commit message: `Iteration X: [brief description]`

#### Step 6: Next Iteration
- Review next iteration requirements
- Agree on proceeding to next iteration
- Repeat workflow from Step 1

## Important Rules

- **Strict Order**: Complete iterations sequentially (1 → 2 → 3...)
- **No Skipping**: Don't move to next iteration until current one is confirmed complete
- **Approval Required**: Always get approval before implementing
- **Confirmation Required**: Wait for confirmation after implementation
- **Update Tasklist**: Keep progress report current
- **Commit Regularly**: Commit after each completed iteration

## Status Updates

When updating [tasklist.md](./tasklist.md) progress report:
- ⬜ Not Started
- 🟡 In Progress (when starting iteration)
- ✅ Complete (when iteration confirmed complete)
- ❌ Blocked (if blocked, document why)

## Code Review Checklist

Before requesting approval:
- [ ] Code follows [conventions.md](../conventions.md)
- [ ] Matches architecture in [vision.md](../vision.md)
- [ ] Test criteria met
- [ ] No unnecessary complexity
- [ ] Error handling in place

